# Shell scripts run on the Linux box (ops/scan.sh is the 2-hourly cron job).
# A CRLF shebang makes them unrunnable — `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` is not a valid
# interpreter — and that is exactly what took the scanner down for 8 weeks in
# Jun–Aug 2026 after a copy from a Windows PC. Force LF regardless of the
# checkout platform's core.autocrlf.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for anything else the box executes or parses line-by-line.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
